# prevent-damage-on-turn at turn 3 against "damage can't be prevented this turn" (CR 615.12): on Bot1's third turn (turn 5)
# the prevention is made at its upkeep, and Bot1's Lightning Bolt at itself is prevented; then Skullcrack's "damage can't
# be prevented this turn" applies, and its own 3 damage to Bot1 is dealt despite the prevention effect. Bot1's second turn
# has no trigger.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain x3
Lightning Bolt
Skullcrack
Mountain x35

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x40

[Variant]
Bot1: emblem Gear test: prevent-damage-on-turn, turn 3

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 0
